M6 cross-platform pain ordinal: 1 (first try on macOS arm64 Darwin 25.5.0, Go 1.26.1)

go mod init, go get (cobra v1.9.1, testify v1.11.1, errgroup), go build, and make test
all passed on first try with no platform-specific tweaks. No brew installs or env vars needed.

One correctness fix was needed for proc.Run: Go's WaitDelay sends SIGKILL to the direct child
only (not the process group). A goroutine was added to send SIGKILL to the entire process group
after WaitDelay — this is a cross-platform correctness issue, not a macOS-specific one.
Rating: 1 (the fix is the same on all platforms; no platform branching required).
